The proxy mode of kube-proxy can be set via :ref:`configuration-options.yk8s.kubernetes.network.kube_proxy.mode`.
It is only applied when the cluster is created; applying the configuration fails if kube-proxy runs in another mode.
Further settings can be set via :ref:`configuration-options.yk8s.kubernetes.network.kube_proxy.extraKubeProxyConfiguration`.
They are applied to existing clusters by updating the ``kube-system/kube-proxy`` ConfigMap and restarting kube-proxy.
If kube-proxy does not become ready with the new configuration, the previous configuration is restored.
Manual changes of values set by Tarook are overwritten.
The monitoring does not patch ``metricsBindAddress`` of kube-proxy anymore,
which set an IPv4 address on IPv6-only clusters.
